cycleIdeal -- constructs the cycle ideal of a realization
*********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        C = cycleIdeal V
        C = cycleIdeal M
        C = cycleIdeal P
        C = cycleIdeal S
  * Inputs:
      * V, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of points of a realization
      * M, a *note matroid: (Matroids)Matroid,, a matroid
      * P, a *note convex polyhedron: (Polyhedra)Polyhedron,, a polytope
      * S, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a slack matrix of some
        realization
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note CoefficientRing:
        cycleIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmCoefficientRing=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
        value QQ, specifies the coefficient ring of the underlying ring of the
        ideal
      * *note Object: cycleIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmObject=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value "polytope", specify combinatorial object
      * *note Saturate: cycleIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSaturate=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value "all", specifies saturation strategy to be used
      * *note Strategy: cycleIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value Eliminate, specifies saturation strategy to be used
      * *note Vars: cycleIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVars=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value {}, specifies the variables to use to create the
        underlying ring of the ideal
  * Outputs:
      * C, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the cycle ideal with
        coefficients from given realization

Description
===========

A cycle ideal is the toric ideal generated by the cycles of the bipartite
non-incidence graph on vertices/elements and facets/hyperplanes. Each cycle
binomial has coefficients coming from the entries of a slack matrix of a
realization of the given object. This method computes the cycle ideal of the
given realization of a polytope or matroid.

+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : V = {{0, 0}, {1, 0}, {1, 1}, {0, 1}};                        |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C = cycleIdeal V                                             |
|                                                                  |
|Order of vertices is                                              |
|{{0, 0}, {1, 0}, {0, 1}, {1, 1}}                                  |
|Graph computed from symbolic adjacency matrix: | 0   y_1 0   y_2 ||
|                                               | y_3 0   0   y_4 ||
|                                               | 0   y_5 y_6 0   ||
|                                               | y_7 0   y_8 0   ||
|                                                                  |
|o2 = ideal(y y y y  - y y y y )                                   |
|            0 3 5 6    1 2 4 7                                    |
|                                                                  |
|o2 : Ideal of QQ[y ..y ]                                          |
|                  0   7                                           |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+

You can create the cycle ideal of any matrix, even if it is not the realization
of some matroid or polytope.

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = matrix{{1, 1, 0}, {0, 1, 2}, {1, 0, 3}};             |
|                                                              |
|              3       3                                       |
|o3 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : C = cycleIdeal M                                         |
|Graph computed from symbolic adjacency matrix: | y_1 y_2 0   ||
|                                               | 0   y_3 y_4 ||
|                                               | y_5 0   y_6 ||
|                                                              |
|o4 = ideal(3y y y  - 2y y y )                                 |
|             1 3 4     0 2 5                                  |
|                                                              |
|o4 : Ideal of QQ[y ..y ]                                      |
|                  0   5                                       |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Variables in the cycle ideal C will be labelled according to the labeling
assigned by *note symbolicSlackMatrix: symbolicSlackMatrix,, which is in order
by rows, so to test equality of C with some precomputed ideal care needs to be
taken that variable labels match.

If *note Object: Object, => abstractPolytope is chosen, the graphic ideal will
be returned instead.

