findFlag -- computes a list of facet labels that make up a flag in a polytope
*****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        F = findFlag P
        F = findFlag M
        F = findFlag S
        F = findFlag V
  * Inputs:
      * P, a *note convex polyhedron: (Polyhedra)Polyhedron,, a polytope
      * M, a *note matroid: (Matroids)Matroid,, a matroid
      * S, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, (symbolic) slack matrix
      * V, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of vertex coordinates,
        matroid vectors, facet labels, or cone generators
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note FlagElement: findFlag_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmFlagElement=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value 0, a facet label that will be contained in a flag of
        facets of given polytope or matroid
      * *note Object: findFlag_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmObject=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value "polytope", specify combinatorial object
  * Outputs:
      * F, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of facet labels or
        hyperplanes or column labels or labels that make up a flag in the given
        polytope or matroid or matrix or object given by V

Description
===========

Given a polytope, a matroid, a cone, it finds a flag of facets or hyperplanes
or cone generators that can be given as input to obtain a reduced slack matrix.

