graphicIdeal -- creates the toric ideal of the non-incidence graph of a polytope
********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        T = graphicIdeal V
        T = graphicIdeal P
        T = graphicIdeal S
        T = graphicIdeal M
  * Inputs:
      * V, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of vertices or of facet
        sets
      * P, a *note convex polyhedron: (Polyhedra)Polyhedron,, a polytope
      * S, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a (symbolic) slack matrix of
        a polytope
      * M, a *note matroid: (Matroids)Matroid,, a matroid
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note CoefficientRing:
        graphicIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmCoefficientRing=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value QQ, specifies the coefficient ring of the underlying ring
        of the ideal
      * *note Object: graphicIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmObject=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value "polytope", specify combinatorial object
      * *note Saturate: graphicIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSaturate=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value "all", specifies saturation strategy to be used
      * *note Strategy: graphicIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value Eliminate, specifies saturation strategy to be used
      * *note Vars: graphicIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVars=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value {}, specifies the variables to use to create the
        underlying ring of the ideal
  * Outputs:
      * T, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the toric ideal of the
        non-incidence graph

Description
===========

The graphic ideal associated to a polytope is the toric ideal of the vector
configuration consisting of the columns of the vertex-edge incidence matrix of
the non-incidence (of vertices and facets) graph of the polytope.

+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = convexHull(matrix{{0, 0, 1, 1}, {0, 1, 0, 1}});          |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : T = graphicIdeal P                                           |
|                                                                  |
|Order of vertices is                                              |
|{{0, 0}, {1, 0}, {0, 1}, {1, 1}}                                  |
|Graph computed from symbolic adjacency matrix: | 0   y_1 0   y_2 ||
|                                               | y_3 0   0   y_4 ||
|                                               | 0   y_5 y_6 0   ||
|                                               | y_7 0   y_8 0   ||
|                                                                  |
|o2 = ideal(y y y y  - y y y y )                                   |
|            0 3 5 6    1 2 4 7                                    |
|                                                                  |
|o2 : Ideal of QQ[y ..y ]                                          |
|                  0   7                                           |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

If S is not a symbolic slack matrix, the ideal will have variables indexed as
in *note symbolicSlackMatrix: symbolicSlackMatrix, (from left to right in order
by rows of S).

See also
========

  * *note graphFromSlackMatrix: graphFromSlackMatrix, -- creates the
    vertex-edge incidence matrix for the bipartite non-incidence graph with
    adjacency matrix the given slack matrix
  * *note cycleIdeal: cycleIdeal, -- constructs the cycle ideal of a
    realization
  * *note symbolicSlackMatrix: symbolicSlackMatrix, -- computes the symbolic
    slack matrix

