slackIdeal -- computes the slack ideal
**************************************

  * Usage: 
        I = slackIdeal(d, V)
        I = slackIdeal M
        I = slackIdeal P
        I = slackIdeal C
        I = slackIdeal V
        I = slackIdeal(d, S)
        I = slackIdeal S
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the dimension of the polytope
        or 1 less than the rank of the matroid
      * V, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of vertices of a polytope,
        the vectors of a linear matroid, or facet sets of an abstract polytope
      * M, a *note matroid: (Matroids)Matroid,, a matroid
      * P, a *note convex polyhedron: (Polyhedra)Polyhedron,, a polytope
      * C, a *note convex rational cone: (Polyhedra)Cone,, a cone
      * S, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a (symbolic) slack matrix
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note CoefficientRing:
        slackIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmCoefficientRing=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
        value QQ, specifies the coefficient ring of the underlying ring of the
        ideal
      * *note Object: slackIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmObject=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value "polytope", specify combinatorial object
      * *note Saturate: slackIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSaturate=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value "all", specifies saturation strategy to be used
      * *note Strategy: slackIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value Eliminate, specifies saturation strategy to be used
      * *note Vars: slackIdeal_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVars=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value {}, specifies the variables to use to create the
        underlying ring of the ideal
  * Outputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the slack ideal - the
        saturated ideal of (d+2)-minors of the symbolic slack matrix

Description
===========

The slack ideal of a d-polytope or rank d+1 matroid is the ideal of
(d+2)-minors of its symbolic slack matrix, saturated by the product of the
variables in the matrix.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : V = {{0, 0}, {1, 0}, {1, 1}, {0, 1}};|
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = slackIdeal V                     |
|                                          |
|Order of vertices is                      |
|{{0, 0}, {1, 0}, {0, 1}, {1, 1}}          |
|                                          |
|o2 = ideal(x x x x  - x x x x )           |
|            0 3 5 6    1 2 4 7            |
|                                          |
|o2 : Ideal of QQ[x ..x ]                  |
|                  0   7                   |
+------------------------------------------+

If a list of points is given it can be treated as the vertices of a polytope,
the ground set of a matroid or the facets of an abstract polytope by specifying
the option *note Object: Object,. The default is as a polytope.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : V = {{0, 0}, {1, 0}, {1, 1}, {0, 1}};                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : IP = slackIdeal V                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|Order of vertices is                                                         |
|{{0, 0}, {1, 0}, {0, 1}, {1, 1}}                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = ideal(x x x x  - x x x x )                                              |
|            0 3 5 6    1 2 4 7                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Ideal of QQ[x ..x ]                                                     |
|                  0   7                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : IM = slackIdeal(V, Object => "matroid")                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = ideal (x x x   + x x x  , x x x  + x x x  , x x x  + x x x  , x x x  +  |
|             4 8 10    5 7 11   1 8 9    2 6 11   0 5 9    2 3 10   0 4 6    |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     x x x , x x x x   - x x x x  , x x x x  - x x x x  , x x x x  -         |
|      1 3 7   1 3 8 10    0 5 6 11   0 4 8 9    2 3 7 11   1 5 7 9           |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     x x x x  )                                                              |
|      2 4 6 10                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : Ideal of QQ[x ..x  ]                                                    |
|                  0   11                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

