symbolicSlackMatrix -- computes the symbolic slack matrix
*********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        S = symbolicSlackMatrix V
        S = symbolicSlackMatrix X
        S = symbolicSlackMatrix M
        S = symbolicSlackMatrix P
        S = symbolicSlackMatrix C
  * Inputs:
      * V, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of points treated as the
        vertices of polytope; or vectors of a linear matroid if matroid is
        given as *note Object: Object,; or a list of indices comprising the
        facets of an abstract polytope if abstractPolytope is given as *note
        Object: Object,.
      * X, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a slack matrix
      * M, a *note matroid: (Matroids)Matroid,, a matroid
      * P, a *note convex polyhedron: (Polyhedra)Polyhedron,, a polytope
      * C, a *note convex rational cone: (Polyhedra)Cone,, a cone
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note CoefficientRing:
        symbolicSlackMatrix_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmCoefficientRing=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value QQ, specifies the coefficient ring of the underlying
        ring of the matrix
      * *note Object: symbolicSlackMatrix_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmObject=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value "polytope", specify combinatorial object
      * *note Vars: symbolicSlackMatrix_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVars=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value {}, specifies the variables to use to create the
        underlying ring of the matrix
  * Outputs:
      * S, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the symbolic slack matrix
        with indexed variables in symbol x

Description
===========

The symbolic slack matrix records the combinatorial structure of the given
object. Its (i, j)-entry is 0 if element i is in hyperplane j and it is a
variable otherwise. Variables are indexed left to right by rows.

