symbolicSlackOfPlucker -- fill the slack matrix with Plücker variables
**********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        fillPl = symbolicSlackOfPlucker(v, B)
        fillPl = symbolicSlackOfPlucker(V, B)
        fillPl = symbolicSlackOfPlucker V
        fillPl = symbolicSlackOfPlucker(S, B)
        fillPl = symbolicSlackOfPlucker S
        fillPl = symbolicSlackOfPlucker P
        fillPl = symbolicSlackOfPlucker M
  * Inputs:
      * v, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, number of polytope vertices,
        cone generators, or matroid vectors
      * B, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, set of hyperplane spanning set
        indices
      * V, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of coordinates for polytope
        vertices, cone generators, or matroid vectors
      * S, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, (symbolic) slack matrix
      * P, a *note convex polyhedron: (Polyhedra)Polyhedron,, a polytope
      * M, a *note matroid: (Matroids)Matroid,, a matroid
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note CoefficientRing:
        symbolicSlackOfPlucker_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmCoefficientRing=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value QQ, specifies the coefficient ring of the underlying
        ring of the matrix
      * *note Object: symbolicSlackOfPlucker_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmObject=>_pd_pd_pd_rp
        , => ..., default value "polytope", specify combinatorial object
  * Outputs:
      * fillPl, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, slack matrix filled with
        Plücker variables

Description
===========

Given the number of polytope vertices, cone generators, or matroid vectors, or
a set of polytope vertices, cone generators, or matroid vectors, or a slack
matrix and a set of set of hyperplane spanning set indices, it fills the slack
matrix with Plücker variables.

